//MCQ

::HDFS Commands::
Which of the following command will create a directory?
{
~hdfs -ds mk /directory-name
=hdfs dfs -mkdir /directory-name
~hdfs -dfs mkdir /directory-name
~hdfs dfs dir /directory-name
}

::HDFS Commands::
Which of the following commands can be used to copy a file from the local machine to HDFS? 
{
=hdfs dfs -copyFromLocal source target-on-HDFS
~hdfs dfs  source target-on-HDFS
~hdfs dfs -cp source target-on-HDFS
~hdfs dfs -mv source target-on-HDFS
}

::HDFS Commands::
Which is the correct way of changing the default replication factor in hdfs.
{
=hadoop fs –setrep –w 3 -R /directory_location
~haDoop Fs -setreps -w 3 -R /directory_location
~hadoop fs –setrep –w 
~None of the above
}

::HDFS Commands::
Which command is used to copy a file existing in HDFS to your local file system?
{
~hdfs dfs -copyFromLocal localLocation remoteLocation
~hdfs dfs -copyToLocal localLocation remoteLocation
=hdfs dfs -copyFromLocal remoteLocation localLocation
~hdfs dfs -copyToLocal remoteLocation localLocation
}

::HDFS Commands::
Which command is used to format the NameNode?
{
~hdfs namenodes -format
~hdfs node -remove
=hdfs namenode -format
~None of the above
}
